rection":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":3.73641e-33,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.410368,"nucleus_score":-12.1575,"pct_ad":0.0774719,"pct_control":0.104136,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.439301,"donor_log2fc":-0.449537,"donor_lfcse":0.16242,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.246239}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000204262","module":"green","kme":0.148616,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.299526,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000204262","module":"black","kme":0.651742,"hub":true,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.391996,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000204262","module":"turquoise","kme":0.117497,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.398013,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000204262","entrez_id":["1290"],"uniprot":["P05997"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes an alpha chain for one of the low abundance fibrillar collagens. Fibrillar collagen molecules are trimers that can be composed of one or more types of alpha chains. Type V collagen is found in tissues containing type I collagen and appears to regulate the assembly of heterotypic fibers composed of both type I and type V collagen. This gene product is closely related to type XI collagen and it is possible that the collagen chains of types V and XI constitute a single collagen type with tissue-specific chain combinations. Mutations in this gene are associated with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome, types I and II. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P05997","text":"Type V collagen is a member of group I collagen (fibrillar forming collagen). It is a minor connective tissue component of nearly ubiquitous distribution. Type V collagen binds to DNA, heparan sulfate, thrombospondin, heparin, and insulin. Type V collagen is a key determinant in the assembly of tissue-specific matrices (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}